winch apply: show the changes, ask, then make them

Examples:
  # plan the pipeline site, ask, and make the changes
  winch apply site
  # apply on the test inventory without the question
  winch apply site --inventory test --yes
  # apply the stage mail on the mail hosts
  winch apply site --hosts mail --stages mail
  # apply only the plan that you checked before
  winch apply site --check a3f9c2e1d07b4c58

Usage:
  winch apply [<pipeline>] [flags]

Apply shows the plan of a pipeline, asks the question "Apply these
changes?", and then makes the changes.

Leave out the pipeline name when the steps are at the top of
winch.yaml.

winch asks only when stdin and stderr are terminals. Without a
terminal, and without --yes or --check, apply prints the plan and exits
with code 5. Its last line is the command that applies the plan with
its hash.

--check replaces the question. When the new plan has another hash,
apply exits with code 6 and changes nothing.

A host pattern is a group or a host, with "," for union, "&" for
intersection, and "!" for exclusion. Each stage runs on the hosts in
both its hosts and --hosts. The stages of --stages run in pipeline
order.

A --set value parses as YAML.

With a terminal, ssh can ask questions, and winch connects to the
hosts one at a time. Without one, or with --batch, ssh asks nothing,
and winch connects to them in parallel. The apply question stays.

The first Ctrl-C lets the running step on each host finish and starts
no new step. A second Ctrl-C ends the sessions at once.

Flags:
  --inventory <name>          inventory for the run
                              default: inventory in winch.yaml
  --hosts <pattern>           only these hosts
                              default: all
  --stages <names>            only these stages, such as mail,monit
                              default: all
  --user [<host>=]<name>      SSH login user, for all hosts or one;
                              repeatable
                              default: from the inventory
  --set vars.<name>=<value>   variable value; repeatable
  --batch                     no questions from ssh
  --yes                       no apply question
  --check <hash>              plan hash that the apply needs
  --json                      JSON events on stdout

See: winch doc workflow, winch doc pipeline, winch doc inventory
